      "writtenOn": "2023-12-12T17:51:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`!state` doesn\u0027t make any sense - it means that keys can\u0027t be created for some reason, probably related to NVMEM and U2F won\u0027t work. It is there only as a safety precaution. If `u2f_get_state()` fails we have something much more serious. So, practically it is only either U2F seeds are FIPS or not FIPS. I can add it if you still think it can be useful.",
      "parentUuid": "73d5ccde_89bfac3f",
      "revId": "00ad6f4d1a92ef88c7120d203b583358faee906d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
